{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Observable.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Observable.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"observable observable","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Observable.md","fileName":"Observable.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Observable","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:31\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[HTTP API Integration]] [[Reactive Programming in .NET]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["HTTP API Integration","Reactive Programming in .NET","Angular HttpClient","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Observable.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Observable.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"observable observable","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Observable.md","fileName":"Observable.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Observable","heading":"Observable","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An observable represents a sequence of values or events that a consumer can subscribe to over time. It fits asynchronous client behavior because the producer can emit a result, an error, or later updates without blocking the caller.\n\nAngular [[Angular HttpClient|HttpClient]] returns observables for HTTP operations. Components and services can transform, retry, or react to those streams, and an activity log can observe form changes without repeatedly polling the form model.\n\n.NET's `IObservable<T>` expresses the producer side of the same general idea: an observer subscribes, receives notifications as values change, and can dispose of the subscription. The inventory example makes a product recorder the provider for several reporting observers, keeping the provider independent of each report's behavior.","tags":["baby"],"links":["HTTP API Integration","Reactive Programming in .NET","Angular HttpClient","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Observable.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Observable.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"observable observable","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Observable.md","fileName":"Observable.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Observable","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf]]\n[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["HTTP API Integration","Reactive Programming in .NET","Angular HttpClient","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}